(4142, 'emphasizes the impressive ability to retain memories for a long time', 'thù dai, nhớ lâu', 1, 3830, 6487, '', 1, 1, '', '', 'based on the belief that elephants have excellent memories. It means that elephants, and metaphorically people who are described this way, can remember things for a long time. In nature, elephants are known for their ability to recall locations, recognize individual elephants and people, and remember events, even after many years. For instance, they may remember where water sources are or who treated them kindly or poorly. When used to describe a person, saying someone has an \"elephant memory\" or that they \"never forget\" implies they have a strong memory, especially for details, past interactions, or events.', ''),
(4143, 'the supply of people who are able to work:', 'nhân lực', 1, 3831, 6488, '', 1, 1, '', '', '', ''),
(4144, '', '', 3, 3832, 6489, 'conscious', 1, 1, '', 'unconscious', '', ''),
(4145, '<ul><li>(of people) having a close and friendly relationship;</li><li>private and personal, often in a sexual way; (of a link between things) very close</li></ul>', '<ul><li>mật thiết, thân thiết (có quan hệ gần gũi với nhau - người hoặc vật)</li><li>thân mật (với ai đó): theo xu hướng sexual relationship</li></ul>', 3, 3010, 6490, '', 1, 1, 'intimate (with sb): having a sexual relationship with sb', '', '', 'intimate friends: bạn bè thân thiết\nintimate connection (between A and B): mối quan mật thiết (giữa A và B)\nbe on intimate terms with sb: thân thiết với ai đó'),
